{"name":"SMV tier-list threads","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":30,"casual":{"lead":["SMV tier-list threads are posts on looksmaxxing forums in which a member ranks items (muscle groups, facial features, procedures, supplements, even ethnic groups) into S/A/B-style tiers. SMV stands for sexual market value, the community's term for overall attractiveness.","For appearance improvement, the lists work as a prioritisation shorthand: a member who sees height and frame near the top of a features list, or a particular surgery rated highly, can decide where to put effort. They are opinion posts, usually followed by replies disputing the placements; the format itself comes from video-game culture."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Members post a list with tier headings, others reply with their own rankings or objections, and popular threads get updated versions. Topics range from muscle SMV and dimorphic features to surgeries, SARMs and anime. Readers use them as a starting point for further research rather than as measurements."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Lists are subjective and often disagree with each other. Some rank medical procedures or performance-enhancing compounds, and the placements reflect the poster's opinion, not clinical guidance. Some threads rank groups of people, which is contentious even within the community."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Meta-optimization for fully automated radiation therapy treatment planning.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35176734/","source":"Physics in medicine and biology","year":2022,"cites":10,"kind":null},{"title":"Decoding molecular markers and transcriptional circuitry of naive and primed states of human pluripotency","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2020.04.17.046037","source":"bioRxiv","year":2020,"cites":0,"kind":null}],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Tier List of Dimorphic Features (MEN)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threa