smax.org/threads/race-tier-list.500063/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220514135417/https://looksmax.org/threads/race-tier-list.500063/"},{"title":"factors of male attractiveness tier list","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/factors-of-male-attractiveness-tier-list.367092/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220521000242/https://looksmax.org/threads/factors-of-male-attractiveness-tier-list.367092/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"SMV tier-list threads — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Tier_list"},{"title":"Sexual market value - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_market_value"},{"title":"Tier list - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tier_list"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Confidence & presence","chain":["Members rank features, muscles or procedures into tiers","Readers see which items the community thinks matter most","They choose where to spend effort on their own appearance"],"effect":"claimed","text":"The lists condense community opinion into a quick ordering of what to work on, such as muscle groups, frame, or surgeries. They are used as a starting point for deciding priorities, with the ranking itself coming from forum consensus and argument."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Tier_list","lead":["SMV tier-list threads are forum posts, mainly on looksmax.org, that rank things related to attractiveness into labelled tiers. 'SMV' stands for sexual market value, a term from pick-up-artist forums that later spread through the wider manosphere and incel-adjacent spaces, where people are rated on decile or 'PSL' scales [1].","The tier-list format began in video-game communities, where players sorted characters by tournament viability; the top 'S' grade echoes Japanese grading [2]. Looksmaxxing forums borrowed it to sort anything from muscle groups to cosmetic surgeries.","For someone trying to look better, these lists serve as a prioritisation map. A 'Tier List of Dimorphic Features (Men)' thread, for example, put height and frame in the top tier, jaw and neck width next, and facial hair and hairline shape in a bottom 'doesn't matter' tier, while replies debated whether height counts as dimorphic [3]. Other threads rank plastic and cosmetic surgeries, SARMs, muscle groups and body features [4][5]. No published study validates these rankings; they record community opinion."],"infobox":[["Type","Forum ranking format"],["Main venue","looksmax.org"],["Format origin","Video-game tier lists"],["Common topics","Muscle SMV, dimorphic features, surgeries, SARMs"],["Basis","Poster opinion and replies"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["A tier list sorts items into ordered groups, typically S, A, B, C and D, from most to least favourable. The format grew out of video-game culture, where players used it for characters and in-game elements, and has spread to films, sports teams and many other subjects, usually to prompt discussion or give a quick overview [2]. Critics of the format point out that it flattens context, a limitation noted by games journalist Maddy Myers regarding team-based games [2].","On looksmaxxing forums the same layout is applied to attractiveness. Examples include threads titled 'muscle SMV tier list', 'plastic surgery tier list', 'softmax tier list', 'updated roidmaxxing tier list for bone mass and masculinization' and a thread tier-listing SARMs with suggested stacks [4][6][7]. Others rank by race or by country, or are jokes such as theme songs [8]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Examples","paras":[],"subs":[{"h":"Features","paras":["One thread on male dimorphic features listed height and frame in tier 1, jaw and neck width in tier 2, chin height and browridge projection in tier 3, occipital shape and nose slope in tier 4, and facial hair and hairline shape in a lowest tier. A reply questioned whether height is dimorphic, and another answered that it is [3]."]},{"h":"Procedures and compounds","paras":["A surgery tier list graded procedures from acceptable to disliked, with the poster giving reasons for each placement; replies mostly tagged other members [9]. A SARMs thread ranked compounds by potency and selectivity and added example stacks, with the author asking readers to correct mistakes [10]. These reflect personal opinion and personal experience, not clinical recommendation."]}]},{"h":"Research and expert views","paras":["No studies of looksmaxxing tier lists as such have been published. Researchers describing SMV note that the concept is a manosphere counterpart to the academic idea of sexual or erotic capital, and the sociological literature on that idea has been criticised for, among other things, understating cultural and social constraints on how attractiveness is valued [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing culture","paras":["Tier-list threads are a common way for newer members to orient themselves, and the replies often become the real content, with members disputing placements or posting their own versions. Updated versions of popular lists circulate over time, and the format is also used humorously [8]."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Members use tier lists as shared shorthand for what matters in appearance, while regularly disputing individual placements [3][9].","claims":[{"claim":"Height and frame sit at the top of male features","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Muscle can be ranked by SMV impact","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Sexual market value","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_market_value","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Tier list (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Tier_list","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Tier List of Dimorphic Features (MEN)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-of-dimorphic-features-men.1382483/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2024,"type":"forum"},{"title":"muscle smv tier list","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/muscle-smv-tier-list.943559/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2023,"type":"forum"},{"title":"softmax tier list","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/softmax-tier-list.1724391/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2024,"type":"forum"},{"title":"plastic surgery tier list","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/plastic-surgery-tier-list.1717150/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2024,"type":"forum"},{"title":"updated roidmaxxing tier list for bone mass and masculinization","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/updated-roidmaxxing-tier-list-for-bone-mass-and-masculinization.1401757/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2024,"type":"forum"},{"title":"looksmaxing theme songs tier list","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/looksmaxing-theme-songs-tier-list.1533967/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2024,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Tier list for surgeries","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-for-surgeries.1119790/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2023,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Tier List and Stacks for SARMS","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-and-stacks-for-sarms-mid-effort.979640/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2023,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Tier List of Dimorphic Features (MEN)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-of-dimorphic-features-men.1382483/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250330182633/https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-of-dimorphic-features-men.1382483/"},{"title":"Tier list for surgeries","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-for-surgeries.1119790/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20241010072714/https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-for-surgeries.1119790/"},{"title":"Tier List and Stacks for SARMS - Mid effort","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tier-list-and-stacks-for-sarms-mid-effort.979640/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":